.TITLE "mkdir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Creates one or more directories. It allows for the creation of __folder structures__ and can set specific __permissions__ during the creation process.

.DIV "TLDR"
**mkdir name**
Creates a new directory with the specified name in the current path.
> __name__ the new directory name

**mkdir -p path/to/folder**
Creates a directory along with any missing parent directories.
> __-p__ parents flag | __path/to/folder__ the nested directory path

**mkdir -m mode name**
Creates a directory with specific octal permissions.
> __-m__ mode flag | __mode__ numeric permissions | __name__ directory name

**mkdir -v name**
Displays a message for every directory created.
> __-v__ verbose flag | __name__ directory name

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __-p__ flag is highly recommended for scripts to avoid errors if a directory already exists. Using __mkdir -m__ ensures a directory is created with the correct security context from the start.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:ls** **linux:chmod**

